>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `BLAST_DEPTH_TAC`

``` hol4
tableauLib.BLAST_DEPTH_TAC : int -> thm list -> tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Solves a goal by classical tableau search at one fixed resource bound.

After built-in preprocessing, `BLAST_DEPTH_TAC n thms` makes one tableau
search with resource limit `n`; it neither iterates through smaller limits
nor consults `tableauLib.depth_limit`. The limit is not a literal formula
depth. Safe non-instantiating inferences are free, while unsafe and
instantiating inferences consume it according to the tableau's branching
penalty. A negative limit disables tableau search, although preprocessing
can still solve a goal. There is no timeout.

The theorem list locally processes `SIntro`, `Intro`, `SElim`, `Elim`,
`SDest`, `Dest` and `Del` markers. Every unmarked theorem is inserted as an
assumption before tableau translation. Content-bearing generic simplifier
wrappers are unwrapped and inserted; inert generic controls are ignored.

Found tableaux are replayed through typed HOL inference. A replay failure
causes internal backtracking. Trace family `"blast"` reports such failures
and rule warnings at level 1, statistics at level 2, and full tableau
states at level 3 and above.

The fixed-bound prover intentionally ignores classical wrappers and reads
only the rule nets. It rejects weak elimination rules whose premises lose
the arbitrary conclusion. Its search unifier is first-order, not
higher-order, so some higher-order rule applications are unavailable.
Equality support is also incomplete: suitable equality assumptions can be
used for restricted substitution, but there is no complete equational
reasoner.

This classical tableau tactic is distinct from `blastLib.BBLAST_TAC`, the
finite-word bit-blasting tactic.

### Failure

Fails unless preprocessing or a reconstructed tableau proof closes the
goal within the specified limit. Marker processing can also fail on
malformed extra rules.

### Example

``` hol4
Theorem blast_depth_tac_example:
  (p \/ q) ==> (p ==> r) ==> (q ==> r) ==> r
Proof
  tableauLib.BLAST_DEPTH_TAC 2 []
QED
```

